# Line endings (2026-11-10): the repo stores LF, and the working copy keeps LF too, whatever core.autocrlf says
# (Python, YAML and CI on Linux all read LF; this ends git's "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on Windows).
* text=auto eol=lf
# Batch files need Windows line endings to run reliably in cmd.exe.
*.bat text eol=crlf
# Data and images: never touched.
*.parquet binary
*.npy binary
*.png binary
*.grib2 binary
